  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research and recently welcomed new team members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray to enhance its machine learning and cloud computing capabilities. The executive board approved a total budget of $2M, which includes specific allocations for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase, with a celebration planned for October 10th. The team is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November, and security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year."
